# Error alerting and notifications

Production error alerts and operational notifications go through a **provider registry** (same pattern as payments/shipping). Telegram is the built-in default.

Relevant modules: [app/libs/alerting/index.server.js](mdc:app/libs/alerting/index.server.js), [app/libs/alerting-types.server.js](mdc:app/libs/alerting-types.server.js), [app/libs/error/index.server.js](mdc:app/libs/error/index.server.js), [app/libs/alerting/telegram.server.js](mdc:app/libs/alerting/telegram.server.js), [app/libs/telegram.server.js](mdc:app/libs/telegram.server.js).

## What to call

| Use case | Import | Notes |
| -------- | ------ | ----- |
| Route/action errors | `handleError` from `#/libs/error/index.server` | Logs + sends `sendErrorAlert` in production |
| Direct error alerts | `sendErrorAlert` from `#/libs/alerting/index.server` | Jobs, bootstrap, background workers |
| General notifications | `sendAlertMessage` from `#/libs/alerting/index.server` | Same provider as errors |
| Custom provider | `registerProvider` from `#/libs/alerting/index.server` | Register at startup (e.g. bootstrap) |

Do **not** call `sendTelegramError` or `sendTelegramMessage` in new code — those legacy helpers were removed. Use the alerting handlers above.

## Configuration

From [`.env.example`](mdc:.env.example):

- `ERROR_ALERT_PROVIDER` — provider id (default: `telegram`)
- `ERROR_ALERTS_ENABLED` — set `false` to disable all alerts/messages
- `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`, `TELEGRAM_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED` — Telegram provider credentials

Alerts and messages are skipped in `NODE_ENV=development`.

## Custom providers

Register a provider that implements `sendError(errorData, options?)`. Optionally implement `sendMessage(message, options?)` for general notifications.

```js
import { registerProvider } from '#/libs/alerting/index.server';

registerProvider('slack', {
  id: 'slack',
  name: 'Slack',
  async sendError(errorData, options) {
    // ...
    return true;
  },
  async sendMessage(message, options) {
    // ...
    return true;
  },
});
```

Then set `ERROR_ALERT_PROVIDER=slack`.

Built-in Telegram adapter: `#/libs/alerting/telegram.server.js` (wraps `#/libs/telegram.server.js`).

## Route errors

In loader/action `catch` blocks, return `handleError` from `#/libs/error/index.server` — do not call alerting handlers directly from routes unless you have a non-HTTP use case.
